      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"RST $00: on at TO_SWAP_BANK7, which swaps SP with the pointer kept at $5B6A and pages RAM\nbank 7 in at $C000 (SP_SWAP_BANK7). Used in pairs with RST $08 around work on the program in\nbank 0."},
        "1": {"comment":"On at TO_SWAP_BANK7"},
        "3": {"synopsis":"Returns DE = $0208, the version of this ROM; NextZXOS ROM 2 calls it at $1D05 (through its\n$3E18) to check the alternate ROM.\nExit: DE = $0208.","comment":"The version"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: on at BANK0_SP_SWAP: RAM bank 0 at $C000 and SP swapped with the pointer kept at\n$5B6A.","comment":"RAM bank 0 and the normal stack"},
        "11": {"synopsis":"RST $00's way on to SP_SWAP_BANK7.","comment":"RAM bank 7 and the alternate stack"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: calls the address in the word after the RST in ROM 0 (CALL_ROM0), then returns past\nthe word.","comment":"A routine in ROM 0"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: calls the address in the word after the RST in ROM 1 (CALL_ROM1), then returns past\nthe word.","comment":"A routine in ROM 1"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: calls the address in the word after the RST in ROM 3 (CALL_ROM3), then returns past\nthe word.","comment":"A routine in ROM 3"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: prints A through the current channel: ROM 3's PRINT_A ($0010) through ROM3_CALL_BC.\nNo inline word. Keeps BC.","comment":"The caller's BC kept"},
        "44": {"comment":"On with ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"The maskable interrupt (IM 1): AF and HL kept, H = 0, A = $80, then INT_DIVMMC.","comment":"AF and HL kept for INT_RETURN"},
        "58": {"comment":"H = 0 for the DivMMC's handler"},
        "60": {"comment":"$80: CONMEM, the DivMMC's memory paged in"},
        "62": {"comment":"On past the filler"},
        "70": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 (DivMMC control) = $80: the DivMMC's memory replaces this ROM at $0000-$3FFF, so\nthe bytes after this OUT are never run here; the DivMMC's handler continues at $0048 and\ncomes back through INT_RETURN.","comment":"The DivMMC's memory replaces this ROM from here"},
        "96": {"synopsis":"The end of the interrupt: HL and AF back, interrupts on, return. Reached from the DivMMC's\nhandler.","comment":"Back here from the DivMMC's handler"},
        "98": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The non-maskable interrupt: RETN at once.","comment":"Nothing done"},
        "104": {"synopsis":"RST $10's work: calls the routine at the word after the RST in ROM 0:\n1. BC = the word, the return address moved past it.\n2. ROM 0's $007B (which pages this ROM back in) as the way back, the routine's address on\n   top.\n3. ALT_ROM_OFF: this ROM paged out, the RET goes into ROM 0. Keeps BC (through $5B54).","comment":"The caller's BC kept while the word is read"},
        "108": {"comment":"HL = the address of the word"},
        "109": {"comment":"BC = the word: the routine's address"},
        "113": {"comment":"The return address past the word; HL back"},
        "114": {"comment":"ROM 0's ALT_ROM_ON, the way back into this ROM"},
        "118": {"comment":"The routine's address for the RET"},
        "119": {"comment":"The caller's BC back"},
        "123": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8C = 0: the alternate ROM off, so the standard ROM appears at $0000; the RET goes\nto the address on the stack there.","comment":"The alternate ROM off: RET into the standard ROM"},
        "128": {"synopsis":"RST $18's work: calls the routine at the word after the RST in ROM 1: BC = the word, the\nreturn address moved past it; ROM 0's $007B as the way back and ROM 0's $3E8A (which selects\nROM 1 and calls BC) as the first stop; then ALT_ROM_OFF. Keeps BC.","comment":"The caller's BC kept while the word is read"},
        "132": {"comment":"HL = the address of the word"},
        "133": {"comment":"BC = the word: the routine's address"},
        "137": {"comment":"The return address past the word; HL back"},
        "138": {"comment":"ROM 0's ALT_ROM_ON, the way back into this ROM"},
        "142": {"comment":"ROM 0's $3E8A selects ROM 1 and goes to BC"},
        "146": {"comment":"Alternate ROM off; RET to $3E8A"},
        "148": {"synopsis":"RST $28's second half: BC = ROM 3's PRINT_A ($0010), then as CALL_ROM3 at ROM3_CALL_BC.","comment":"BC = ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "182": {"synopsis":"RST $20's work: calls the routine at the word after the RST in ROM 3 (ROM3_CALL_BC with BC =\nthe word, the return address moved past it).","comment":"The caller's BC kept while the word is read"},
        "186": {"comment":"HL = the address of the word"},
        "187": {"comment":"BC = the word: the routine's address"},
        "191": {"comment":"The return address past the word; HL back"},
        "192": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at BC in ROM 3: the stack gets ROM 0's $007B (back into this ROM), $5B4D\n(ROM 0 selected again), the routine and $5B48 (ROM 3 selected); the caller's BC back from\n$5B54; then ALT_ROM_OFF.","comment":"ROM 0's ALT_ROM_ON, the last way back"},
        "196": {"comment":"$5B4D: ROM 0 selected again on return"},
        "200": {"comment":"The routine's address"},
        "201": {"comment":"$5B48: ROM 3 selected first"},
        "205": {"comment":"The caller's BC back"},
        "211": {"synopsis":"RST $08's work: RAM bank 0 at $C000 with ROM 0 selected (NextReg $8E = $08), then the SP\nswap: SP exchanged with the pointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved to the new\nstack.\nChanges: AF' only.","comment":"RAM bank 0 at $C000, ROM 0 selected"},
        "215": {"comment":"AF kept in AF'"},
        "216": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "217": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "220": {"comment":"HL = the other stack's pointer"},
        "223": {"comment":"This stack's pointer kept in its place"},
        "227": {"comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "228": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "231": {"comment":"The return address onto the new stack"},
        "232": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "233": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "234": {"synopsis":"RST $00's work: SP exchanged with the pointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved to the\nnew stack, then RAM bank 7 at $C000 with ROM 0 selected (NextReg $8E = $78).\nChanges: AF' only.","comment":"AF kept in AF'"},
        "235": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "236": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "239": {"comment":"HL = the other stack's pointer"},
        "242": {"comment":"This stack's pointer kept in its place"},
        "246": {"comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "247": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "250": {"comment":"The return address onto the new stack"},
        "251": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "252": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, ROM 0 selected"},
        "257": {"synopsis":"Looks A up in the table at HL (entries of a byte and a routine address, ended by $FF) and\njumps to the routine of the entry whose byte is A, with RET_Z_SET as its way back.\nEntry: A = the value, HL = the table.\nExit: found, the routine's flags with Z set (H = 0), HL past the entry; not found, carry\nclear and NZ, BC, DE and HL kept.","comment":"RET_Z_SET, where the routine returns"},
        "263": {"synopsis":"One entry: B = its byte, DE = its address.","comment":"B = the entry's byte"},
        "264": {"comment":"The $FF end?"},
        "267": {"comment":"B back"},
        "268": {"comment":"DE = the entry's routine"},
        "272": {"comment":"HL = the next entry"},
        "273": {"comment":"A's entry?"},
        "276": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "278": {"synopsis":"The $FF end: carry clear, NZ, the pushed RET_Z_SET dropped.","comment":"No carry"},
        "279": {"comment":"NZ ($FF)"},
        "282": {"comment":"RET_Z_SET dropped"},
        "284": {"synopsis":"Found: the routine's address goes on the stack, DE back."},
        "285": {"comment":"HL = the routine, DE = past the entry"},
        "286": {"comment":"The routine for the RET; HL = the caller's DE"},
        "287": {"comment":"DE back; HL past the entry"},
        "288": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "289": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at HL, then returns with Z set and H = 0. No caller in this page.","comment":"The routine at HL"},
        "292": {"synopsis":"H = 0 and Z set: where TABLE_DISPATCH's routines return.","comment":"H = 0"},
        "294": {"comment":"Z set"},
        "296": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL here calls the routine at HL.","comment":"A CALL here calls HL"},
        "297": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the editing rows (window rows 0 to ($D73C), bank 7 from $C000) from the program and\ndraws them, the cursor going to E_PPC's line when it is among them:\n1. $D741 bit 1 set (E_PPC looked for), bit 0 cleared; in a mode other than 0 ($D5B8) E_PPC =\n   0.\n2. ROWS_REBUILD_GO: with E_PPC 0, $D5B5 = 0.\n3. The rows above the window emptied ($0DC3) and refilled with as many rows as before\n   ($CE73), from the line before ($D74E) on ($13F9); the rows below emptied (BELOW_RESET).\n4. Each window row taken from the program (ROW_FROM_BELOW); on E_PPC's first row the cursor\n   is placed ($D5B5) places on.\n5. E_PPC not found: $D74E = E_PPC, the rows above emptied, again; E_PPC 0: the line $1401\n   gives becomes E_PPC, again.\n6. The rows drawn (RB_DRAW).","comment":"No E_PPC row found yet"},
        "302": {"comment":"E_PPC looked for"},
        "304": {"comment":"Mode ($D5B8) not 0?"},
        "310": {"comment":"Then E_PPC = 0"},
        "316": {"synopsis":"Again from here (RB_AGAIN), with E_PPC changed.","comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "319": {"comment":"E_PPC 0?"},
        "323": {"comment":"Then no places to move the cursor on"},
        "326": {"synopsis":"The count of rows above the window kept; $D74C = the line before $D74E ($13F9); both buffers\nemptied.","comment":"A = the count of rows above the window"},
        "329": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "333": {"comment":"The line before it"},
        "336": {"comment":"Kept at $D74C"},
        "339": {"comment":"The rows above emptied"},
        "342": {"comment":"The rows below emptied"},
        "345": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "346": {"synopsis":"One row from the program put above the window, until the count is used up.","comment":"None left?"},
        "349": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "350": {"comment":"The next row from the program"},
        "353": {"comment":"DE = the row"},
        "354": {"comment":"Put above the window"},
        "357": {"comment":"One less"},
        "361": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to ($D73C): B = the row, C = ($D73C), DE = the row's place; the two kept on the\nstack.","comment":"Row 0"},
        "363": {"comment":"DE = its place"},
        "366": {"comment":"B = 0, the first row"},
        "367": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "371": {"comment":"Both kept"},
        "373": {"synopsis":"One row: the next from the program (ROW_FROM_BELOW); while E_PPC is looked for, is this\nE_PPC's first row?","comment":"HL = the next row from the program"},
        "376": {"comment":"E_PPC looked for?"},
        "385": {"comment":"DE = the width"},
