        "3239": {"comment":"Deleted"},
        "3243": {"comment":"Again"},
        "3245": {"synopsis":"The start of a deleting key: $D5B7 bit 0 cleared, the cursor loaded and taken off the screen\n(CURSOR_OFF), $D741 bit 2 set (no drawing while rows move).\nExit: HL = $D748; C, B, A as CURSOR_GET.","comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "3248": {"comment":"The rows not full any more"},
        "3250": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "3253": {"comment":"HL = $D741"},
        "3256": {"comment":"No drawing while rows move"},
        "3258": {"comment":"HL = $D748"},
        "3262": {"synopsis":"Is the cursor (row C, column B) at the start of its line's text? Z when row C is the line's\nfirst row (flags bit 0) and B is 0 or the character before B is 0.\nExit: Z or NZ (A = 1).","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3265": {"comment":"HL = the width"},
        "3268": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "3269": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3273": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3274": {"comment":"Column 0: Z"},
        "3276": {"comment":"The column before"},
        "3277": {"comment":"A = its character"},
        "3280": {"comment":"The column back"},
        "3281": {"comment":"None: Z"},
        "3283": {"synopsis":"NZ.","comment":"A = 1"},
        "3285": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "3287": {"synopsis":"DE = the address of row C of the editor's window, the rows from $C000 in bank 7, ($D73F)\nbytes each: ($D73D) columns of characters, a flags byte, the line number (high byte first).\nKeeps AF, BC.","comment":"The window's rows in bank 7"},
        "3290": {"synopsis":"DE = HL + ($D73F) x C: row C of the rows from HL (BELOW_ROW_ADDR for $C73B, $0E5E for\n$CE76).\nExit: HL = ($D73F). Keeps AF, BC."},
        "3291": {"comment":"A = the row"},
        "3292": {"comment":"DE = the row size"},
        "3296": {"synopsis":"One row size for each row.","comment":"Row 0?"},
        "3299": {"comment":"One row on"},
        "3300": {"comment":"One less"},
        "3303": {"synopsis":"DE = the row.","comment":"DE = the row"},
        "3306": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Keeps DE. No caller in this\npage."},
        "3307": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3310": {"comment":"HL = column B's address"},
        "3316": {"synopsis":"$C738 = 0: no rows kept below the window.","comment":"No rows below the window"},
        "3321": {"synopsis":"Takes the next row from those kept below the window (rows from $C73B, count at $C738): with\nrows kept, $D5B7 bit 0 cleared and the rows shifted up one, the first given; with none, the\nnext program line after ($D74C) (from $1401; line 0 tried as 1) turned into rows ($0E64),\nthe first given and the rest kept.\nExit: HL = $C73B, the row; carry from the routine that made it. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3323": {"comment":"HL = the count of rows below"},
        "3326": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3327": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "3328": {"comment":"Any rows?"},
        "3331": {"comment":"Kept"},
