        "3411": {"comment":"$1881"},
        "3414": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "3415": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "3418": {"comment":"None?"},
        "3420": {"comment":"Then the line last taken"},
        "3423": {"synopsis":"No line before: $D74C kept."},
        "3425": {"synopsis":"A line's first row (bit 0) empties the buffer.","comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3427": {"comment":"HL = the count of rows below"},
        "3430": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3431": {"comment":"No: the row kept"},
        "3433": {"comment":"Count 0: the buffer emptied"},
        "3434": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "3435": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3437": {"synopsis":"Not a first row: put in front when there is room.","comment":"C = the count"},
        "3438": {"comment":"Room for one more?"},
        "3441": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "3442": {"comment":"No room: no carry"},
        "3444": {"comment":"BC = the row size"},
        "3448": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's row 0"},
        "3451": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the row"},
        "3452": {"comment":"The row copied in"},
        "3454": {"comment":"DE = the row size"},
        "3458": {"comment":"The buffer's size"},
        "3461": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "3462": {"comment":"Less one row"},
        "3464": {"comment":"BC = the bytes to move"},
        "3466": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's last byte"},
        "3469": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3470": {"comment":"Less one row"},
        "3472": {"comment":"DE = the last byte"},
        "3473": {"comment":"The rows moved down one"},
        "3475": {"comment":"One row more"},
        "3476": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "3477": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3479": {"synopsis":"Carries character A, pushed off the end of the window's last row (HL = that row's flags\nbyte), into the rows below the window, row 1 on: each row takes it at its text's start\n(ROW_PUSH_CHAR) and passes on what falls off its end; when nothing more falls off, the count\n= C and row C ends the line (bit 3). A row that ended the line gets a new row after it\n(cleared from column B, flags 8, its first ($D7D8) columns cleared); a full buffer ($0EEE)\nsets $D5B7 bit 0 (the rows are full).","comment":"Row 1"},
        "3482": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3484": {"comment":"DE = row 1 below the window"},
        "3487": {"comment":"HL = the last row's flags byte"},
        "3488": {"comment":"Was it the line's last row?"},
        "3490": {"comment":"Not any more"},
        "3492": {"comment":"Yes: a new row needed"},
        "3494": {"synopsis":"B moved over the row's empty cells (TEXT_FROM_COL).","comment":"From column 0"},
        "3496": {"comment":"B = the start of the row's text"},
        "3499": {"synopsis":"A inserted at column B of row DE (ROW_PUSH_CHAR).","comment":"The character back"},
        "3500": {"comment":"In at column B"},
        "3504": {"comment":"The character pushed off kept"},
        "3505": {"comment":"Flags: B added"},
        "3508": {"comment":"Gone through"},
        "3511": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte, DE = the row"},
        "3512": {"comment":"The character back"},
        "3513": {"comment":"Nothing pushed off: done"},
        "3515": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3517": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3518": {"comment":"Room for it?"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "3524": {"comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "3527": {"comment":"The rows full"},
        "3530": {"synopsis":"The row marked as continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared); DE = row C; a row that was not\ncontinued is made new.","comment":"Was the row continued?"},
        "3532": {"comment":"Continued now"},
        "3534": {"comment":"Not the line's last row"},
        "3536": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3539": {"comment":"Continued: into that row"},
        "3543": {"comment":"The row cleared from column B"},
        "3546": {"comment":"Flags 8: the line's last row"},
        "3550": {"comment":"Its first ($D7D8) columns cleared"},
        "3553": {"comment":"In at column B"},
        "3555": {"synopsis":"Nothing more pushed off: the count = C, bit 3 on row C's flags.","comment":"A = the row"},
        "3556": {"comment":"The count of rows below"},
        "3559": {"comment":"The line's last row"},
        "3562": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the rows below the window: $C73B + ($D73F) x C (ROW_ADDRESS_HL).\nExit: HL = ($D73F). Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the rows below the window"},
        "3565": {"comment":"DE = row C of them"},
        "3568": {"synopsis":"Pulls the rows below the window one character back, from the last row ($C738) up to row 1:\nin each row the character at its text's start is taken out (ROW_PULL_CHAR) with the one\ncarried put in at its end. A row left empty is dropped: its flags go to the row before (row\nC - 1, or for row 1 the window's last row), bit 1 cleared there, and the count drops.\nExit: A = the character taken from row 1; carry. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3570": {"comment":"HL = $D5B7"},
        "3573": {"comment":"The rows not full any more"},
        "3575": {"comment":"A = the count of rows below"},
        "3578": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "3579": {"comment":"None?"},
        "3580": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "3582": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "3584": {"synopsis":"Row C: DE = its address; its first used column found (TEXT_FROM_COL).","comment":"DE = row C below the window"},
        "3587": {"comment":"The character carried kept"},
        "3588": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3590": {"comment":"Text in the row from column 0 ($09A2)?"},
        "3593": {"comment":"No: the row dropped"},
        "3595": {"comment":"The character from the row below in at the end ($02C9)"},
        "3596": {"comment":"Its first character out, A in at the end"},
        "3599": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out at column B; still text?"},
        "3601": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3603": {"comment":"Any text left?"},
        "3607": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "3609": {"synopsis":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before.","comment":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before"},
        "3610": {"comment":"A = the dropped row's flags"},
        "3613": {"comment":"Row 1 of the buffer?"},
        "3614": {"comment":"Row 1?"},
        "3618": {"comment":"Then the row before is the window's last ($D73C)"},
        "3621": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "3622": {"comment":"DE = the window's last row"},
        "3625": {"comment":"On"},
        "3627": {"synopsis":"The row before: row C - 1 of the buffer.","comment":"Else row C - 1 of the buffer"},
        "3628": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "3631": {"synopsis":"The row before: bit 1 cleared, the dropped row's flags added; the count one less."},
        "3633": {"comment":"HL = the row before's flags byte"},
        "3636": {"comment":"HL = the flags byte"},
        "3637": {"comment":"Not continued; the dropped row's flags added"},
        "3639": {"comment":"The dropped row's flags added"},
        "3641": {"comment":"One row fewer below the window"},
        "3644": {"comment":"One less"},
        "3645": {"synopsis":"The row above, until row 1 is done.","comment":"A = the character to carry"},
        "3646": {"comment":"The row above, until row 1 is done"},
        "3647": {"comment":"Until row 1 is done"},
        "3649": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "3650": {"synopsis":"DE and BC back; return (with carry when the rows moved, from $0DBB; as entered from $0D78)."},
        "3653": {"synopsis":"ABOVE_INIT's bytes for COPY_COUNTED ($045A): a count (3), then $00 for $CE73 (the count of\nrows kept above the window) and $CE76 for $CE74-$CE75 (the pointer past the top row)."},
        "3657": {"synopsis":"Empties the stack of rows kept above the window: $CE73 (the count) = 0 and $CE74 (the\npointer past the top row) = $CE76, the stack's first row, copied from ABOVE_INIT_DATA by\nCOPY_COUNTED ($045A). From $0136, $01F9 and $0369.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The bytes, a count first"},
        "3660": {"comment":"To $CE73-$CE75"},
        "3666": {"synopsis":"Takes the row nearest the window off the stack of rows above it ($CE73 the count, $CE74 the\npointer past the top row, rows ($D73F) bytes long from $CE76):\n1. With rows on the stack: the pointer moves back one row and the count goes down by one.\n2. With none: the program line before line ($D74E) is found (EXPAND_INIT, PREV_LINE_NUM);\n   when there is one, $D74E = its number, it is written into rows from $CE76 (LINE_TO_ROWS)\n   and its last row is the one taken, the others staying on the stack.\nExit: carry and HL = the row's address; no carry when there is no row. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3668": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "3671": {"comment":"Kept for ABOVE_STORE"},
        "3672": {"comment":"Rows on the stack?"},
        "3676": {"comment":"None: the expansion reset"},
        "3691": {"synopsis":"BC = the line found (or 0)."},
        "3693": {"comment":"HL = $CE76, the stack's first row"},
        "3694": {"comment":"HL = $CE76"},
        "3697": {"comment":"No line: no carry"},
        "3699": {"comment":"HL = $CE73 again"},
        "3702": {"comment":"The line into rows from $CE76; A = the rows"},
        "3705": {"comment":"The last row taken off: count = rows - 1, DE = it"},
        "3706": {"comment":"DE = the line's last row"},
        "3709": {"synopsis":"A row off the stack: the pointer back by one row (($D73F) bytes).","comment":"The pointer past the top row"},
        "3712": {"comment":"BC = the row length"},
        "3718": {"comment":"Carry; the count one less"},
        "3720": {"synopsis":"With carry: the count = A and the pointer = DE.\nExit: HL = DE; BC, DE back."},
        "3721": {"comment":"HL = $CE73, the count"},
        "3722": {"comment":"No carry: nothing stored"},
        "3724": {"comment":"The count stored"},
        "3725": {"synopsis":"The pointer = DE."},
        "3726": {"comment":"The pointer stored"},
        "3729": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "3730": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "3733": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE on the stack of rows above the window ($CE73):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, its line number (the two bytes after the\n   flags, high byte first) goes to $D74E.\n2. A line's last row (flags bit 3) empties the stack instead: $D74E becomes the number of\n   the line after it (EXPAND_INIT, NEXT_LINE_NUM; 0 when there is none), the count 0 and the\n   pointer $CE76.\n3. Otherwise the row is copied on top when one more fits (ROWS_FIT) and the count goes up; a\n   full stack keeps it out.\nExit: carry when the stack changed. Keeps BC, DE."},
        "3735": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "3738": {"comment":"The flags byte"},
        "3740": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "3743": {"comment":"Not both: no line number taken"},
        "3747": {"comment":"Its line number, high byte first"},
        "3755": {"comment":"HL = the flags, DE = the row again"},
        "3757": {"synopsis":"A line's last row (bit 3) empties the stack."},
        "3759": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "3763": {"comment":"Not a last row: kept on the stack"},
        "3766": {"comment":"The expansion reset"},
        "3779": {"comment":"HL = $CE76; count 0, carry"},
        "3782": {"comment":"Count 0, carry: stored"},
        "3786": {"synopsis":"The row copied on top, when there is room.","comment":"C = the count"},
        "3787": {"comment":"One more row fits?"},
        "3790": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "3791": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "3793": {"comment":"The count + 1"},
        "3794": {"comment":"The row copied to the pointer"},
        "3797": {"comment":"BC = the row length"},
        "3801": {"comment":"From the row at DE"},
        "3804": {"comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "3805": {"comment":"Carry: count and pointer stored"},
        "3808": {"synopsis":"Full: the row is not kept."},
        "3809": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "3812": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the stack above the window: $CE76 + ($D73F) x C (ROW_ADDRESS_HL at $0C54).\nKeeps AF, BC. From $08FE and $0B41."},
        "3815": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL"},
        "3818": {"synopsis":"Writes the program line being expanded (EXPAND_NEXT; set up by NEXT_LINE_START or\nPREV_LINE_START) into editor rows from HL + 3, BC its line number:\n1. The first row's flags = $21 (bits 0 and 5) and the number after them, high byte first.\n2. Each character goes in at column B (ROW_PUT_CHAR). A keyword's characters (B = 1 from\n   EXPAND_NEXT) are stored as codes: a letter less $3B, '#' or '$' less $1F, and the R of\n   REM ($D760 = $EA) as 3.\n3. A full row ends with its flags XOR $12 (ROW_NEW) and the next is indented (ROW_INDENT);\n   no room ends the line.\n4. ENTER, or the end of the text, ends the row (ROW_END_LINE; ROW_END_EMPTY for a line with\n   no text).\nWith the state byte ($D5B8) not 0 no text is read.\nExit: carry, HL = the first row, A = the rows.\nChanges: BC, DE.","comment":"DE = HL + 3, the first row"},
        "3823": {"comment":"Kept: the first row"},
        "3824": {"comment":"HL = its flags byte"},
        "3828": {"comment":"The line's first row, a statement starting"},
        "3830": {"comment":"The line number after the flags"},
        "3834": {"comment":"Column 0, one row"},
        "3837": {"synopsis":"The next character, unless the state byte ($D5B8) is not 0."},
        "3839": {"comment":"The state byte"},
        "3843": {"comment":"EXPAND_NEXT: carry, A = a character"},
        "3846": {"comment":"Z: a keyword's character"},
        "3847": {"comment":"DE, BC back; the flags kept"},
        "3849": {"comment":"Carry: a character came"},
        "3851": {"comment":"Nothing on a single row?"},
        "3854": {"comment":"Text written: ROW_END_LINE"},
        "3856": {"comment":"An empty line"},
        "3859": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3861": {"synopsis":"The line's end: the row ended (ROW_END_LINE)."},
        "3864": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3866": {"synopsis":"A character: a keyword's (Z) is stored as a code."},
        "3868": {"comment":"An R"},
        "3870": {"comment":"Another letter"},
        "3875": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "3877": {"comment":"Otherwise 'R' less $3B"},
        "3879": {"comment":"Not after REM"},
        "3881": {"comment":"REM's R: 3"},
        "3883": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3885": {"synopsis":"A keyword's other characters: a letter less $3B, '#' or '$' less $1F."},
        "3887": {"comment":"A letter"},
        "3889": {"comment":"'#' or '$': less $1F"},
        "3891": {"synopsis":"Text: ENTER ends the line."},
        "3893": {"comment":"ENTER: the line's end"},
        "3895": {"synopsis":"Room left in the row?"},
        "3896": {"comment":"The last column"},
        "3901": {"comment":"Column B not past it: stored"},
        "3903": {"comment":"Full: continued, a new row"},
        "3905": {"comment":"ROW_NEW with bits 1 and 4 flipped"},
        "3908": {"comment":"Room: the new row indented"},
        "3910": {"comment":"No room: the line ends"},
        "3913": {"synopsis":"The new row indented."},
        "3916": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B; the next."},
        "3920": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "3922": {"synopsis":"HL = the first row, A = the rows; carry."},
        "3923": {"comment":"A = the rows"},
        "3927": {"synopsis":"Ends row DE (ROW_CLEAR_REST) with its flags XOR A and starts the next: the row's syntax\nstate at its end (ROW_END_STATE) becomes the next row's flags, C + 1, DE + ($D73F).\nExit: carry, HL = the new row's flags byte; no carry when no more rows fit (ROWS_FIT).\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "3928": {"comment":"The rest of the row cleared"},
        "3932": {"comment":"Its flags XOR A"},
        "3933": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "3934": {"comment":"HL = the row, for ROW_END_STATE"},
        "3935": {"comment":"B = the state at the row's end"},
        "3938": {"comment":"DE = the row again"},
        "3939": {"comment":"Room for another row?"},
        "3942": {"comment":"No room: no carry"},
        "3943": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3944": {"comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "3949": {"comment":"Its flags = the state carried on"},
        "3954": {"comment":"Carry: a new row"},
        "3956": {"synopsis":"Do C + 1 rows of ($D73F) bytes fit in $0738 bytes, the size of each row buffer? Exit: carry\nwhen they do. Keeps BC, DE, HL."},
        "3958": {"comment":"E = the row length"},
        "3962": {"comment":"D = C + 1"},
        "3964": {"comment":"DE = (C + 1) x row length"},
        "3966": {"comment":"The buffer's size"},
        "3970": {"comment":"Do they fit?"},
        "3972": {"comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "3974": {"comment":"Carry: they fit"},
        "3976": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of the program line after line HL (HL = 0: the first line) for\nEXPAND_NEXT: EXPAND_INIT, then with bank 0 the line numbered HL found (LINE_FIND_EXACT) and\nthe one after it taken; on to LINE_START_SET. From NEXT_LINE_NUM.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry when there is no such line\n(or no line after it). Bank 7 on exit."},
        "3977": {"comment":"The expansion reset; RAM routines copied"},
        "3980": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "3981": {"comment":"Bank 0: the program"},
        "3982": {"comment":"Line HL there?"},
        "3985": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "3989": {"comment":"HL = 0: the first line itself"},
        "3993": {"comment":"Else the line after it"},
        "3996": {"comment":"Is there one?"},
        "3999": {"comment":"None after it: no carry"},
        "4001": {"synopsis":"For the line at HL: DE = its number (high byte first), then LINE_START_NUM."},
        "4002": {"comment":"DE = the line number"},
        "4004": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "4005": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of a line, DE its number and HL its address + 1: the number as four\ncharacters at $D767 (LINE_NUM_DIGIT; leading zeros as 0 bytes), then $A0 (a space, the\nlast); $D765 = $D767, the text to give first; $D763 = HL + 3, the line's text. From $1A0A\nand $1A27 too.\nExit: carry, HL = the number, DE = the line's text. Keeps IX."},
        "4007": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "4017": {"comment":"HL = the number; no digit seen yet"},
        "4020": {"comment":"Thousands"},
        "4023": {"comment":"The digit for 1000s"},
        "4026": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "4032": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "4038": {"comment":"Units"},
        "4044": {"comment":"A space with bit 7: the text's end"},
        "4048": {"comment":"IX, HL, DE back"},
        "4052": {"comment":"HL = the line's text"},
        "4058": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "4059": {"comment":"Carry: set up"},
        "4061": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 again; the flags as they are."},
        "4062": {"comment":"Flags as they were"},
        "4063": {"synopsis":"One decimal digit of HL into (IX), DE being minus its place's value (-1000, -100, -10, -1):\na 0 before any other digit is stored as 0 (B = 0), later ones as '0' (B = 1).\nExit: HL keeps the rest, IX + 1."},
        "4064": {"synopsis":"DE added while it fits; A counts."},
        "4065": {"comment":"A counts the subtractions"},
        "4066": {"comment":"While HL stays positive"},
        "4068": {"comment":"One too many: back"},
        "4070": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "4071": {"comment":"The digit as a character"},
        "4073": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "4076": {"comment":"A '0'"},
        "4078": {"comment":"A digit 1-9: digits from now on"},
        "4080": {"comment":"Before any other digit?"},
        "4082": {"comment":"A digit seen before: '0' kept"},
        "4084": {"comment":"Then a 0 byte"},
        "4087": {"comment":"Leading zero stored as 0"},
        "4089": {"synopsis":"B = 1: zeros from now on are digits."},
        "4091": {"synopsis":"The next place."},
        "4094": {"synopsis":"As NEXT_LINE_START, for the program line before line HL (bank 0 while it looks; no\nEXPAND_INIT here). From PREV_LINE_NUM.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry when line HL is not found,\nis the first line, or the line before it is numbered 0."},
        "4095": {"comment":"Line HL found? DE = the line before"},
        "4098": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "4100": {"comment":"HL = the line before"},
        "4101": {"comment":"Numbered 0?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"Line 0: no carry"},
        "4107": {"comment":"None before (HL = 0)?"},
        "4110": {"comment":"There is one: set it up"},
        "4113": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "4114": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "4116": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the line after the line at HL (its length added to its start + 4), DE =\nthe line at HL.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4117": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "4119": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "4122": {"comment":"HL = its text"},
        "4123": {"comment":"Past its text"},
        "4124": {"comment":"DE = the line"},
        "4126": {"synopsis":"Is HL on a line? Carry when the byte there has bits 6 and 7 clear (a line number's high\nbyte, not the end of the program).\nChanges: AF."},
        "4127": {"comment":"Bits 6 and 7 of the number's high byte"},
        "4129": {"comment":"Clear: carry"},
        "4131": {"comment":"Set: no carry"},
        "4133": {"synopsis":"Compares the line number at HL (high byte first) with BC.\nExit: carry and Z when they are equal; no carry and NZ when not. Keeps HL."},
        "4134": {"comment":"The high bytes"},
        "4135": {"comment":"Different: no carry"},
        "4136": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "4140": {"comment":"Different: no carry"},
        "4141": {"comment":"Equal: carry"},
        "4143": {"synopsis":"Finds the program line numbered HL (BC = HL) from PROG ($5C53); the program must be paged\nin. BC = 0 takes the first line.\nExit: carry, Z and HL = the line, DE = the line before it (0 for the first); no carry when\nthere is none, DE = the last line.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4144": {"comment":"BC = the number wanted"},
        "4145": {"comment":"No line before yet"},
        "4148": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "4151": {"comment":"A program at all?"},
        "4154": {"comment":"No program: no carry"},
        "4155": {"comment":"The first line numbered 0?"},
        "4159": {"comment":"Numbered 0: on to the next"},
        "4161": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "4164": {"comment":"It is: carry"},
        "4165": {"comment":"Line 0 wanted: the first line"},
        "4168": {"comment":"Line 0 wanted: the first line"},
        "4169": {"synopsis":"The next line, until the end or the one numbered BC."},
        "4172": {"comment":"Still in the program?"},
        "4175": {"comment":"The end: no carry, DE = the last line"},
        "4176": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "4181": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "4182": {"synopsis":"ROW_SETUP's bytes for COPY_COUNTED ($045A): a count (2), then 1 for $D7D7 and 5 for $D7D8."},
        "4185": {"synopsis":"$D7D7 = 1 and $D7D8 = 5 (the cells a line's later rows are indented by, ROW_INDENT), copied\nfrom ROW_SETUP_DATA by COPY_COUNTED ($045A). From $0348.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "4194": {"synopsis":"Puts A in column B of row DE; B + 1.\nChanges: HL."},
        "4197": {"comment":"HL = column B's cell"},
        "4199": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "4201": {"synopsis":"Ends a line's text in row DE: the rest of the row cleared (ROW_CLEAR_REST), its flags' bits\n3 and 4 set, $D7D7 bit 0 set.\nExit: carry, NZ."},
        "4204": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4: the line's last row"},
        "4227": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's cells from column B to the last ($D73D, the column count) to 0.\nExit: B = the column count, HL = the row's flags byte, Z.","comment":"HL = column B's cell"},
        "4231": {"comment":"A = the column count"},
        "4234": {"synopsis":"Up to the last column."},
        "4235": {"comment":"Done: Z"},
        "4236": {"comment":"Cleared; the next"},
        "4245": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4247": {"synopsis":"One cell."},
        "4254": {"comment":"Until the indent is done"},
        "4258": {"synopsis":"Unless $D741 bit 2 is set (no screen output): SCROLL_UP with E = C, which moves window lines\nB + 1 to C one line up and prints the row at HL on line C. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4262": {"comment":"Screen output off?"},
        "4267": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4271": {"comment":"SCROLL_UP with E = C"},
        "4274": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back."},
        "4278": {"synopsis":"Unless $D741 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_DOWN with E = C, which moves window lines B to C - 1 one\nline down and prints the row at HL on line B. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4282": {"comment":"Screen output off?"},
        "4287": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4291": {"comment":"SCROLL_DOWN with E = C"},
        "4294": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back."},
        "4298": {"synopsis":"Marks the cell at column B, line C: WIN_CURSOR_ON with B and C swapped for it. Keeps all\nregisters."},
        "4302": {"comment":"B = line, C = column"},
        "4308": {"comment":"All back"},
        "4313": {"synopsis":"Takes the mark CELL_CURSOR_ON made off the cell at column B, line C (WIN_CURSOR_OFF). Keeps\nall registers."},
        "4317": {"comment":"B = line, C = column"},
        "4323": {"comment":"All back"},
        "4328": {"synopsis":"The editor's window for the main screen, copied to $D7D9 (IX) by WINDOW_SET: a count (8),\nthen 0, 0 (its top line), 20 (its last row, from the top) and five 0s."},
        "4337": {"synopsis":"The window for the lower screen: a count (8), then 0, 22 (its top line), 1 (its last row)\nand five 0s."},
        "4361": {"comment":"COPY_COUNTED"},
        "4364": {"synopsis":"IX + 6 = the cursor's kind from ROM 0's CURSOR_KIND (from MODE, or caps lock), the index\ninto the cursor colours at $D6E8 (CURSOR_KIND_PUT). Keeps AF. From $0482, $051C and $054C."},
        "4365": {"comment":"ROM 0's CURSOR_KIND: A = the kind"},
        "4368": {"comment":"IX + 6 = it"},
        "4373": {"synopsis":"IX + 6 = A; carry."},
        "4378": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at line B of the window (IX + 1 added), column C: the attribute there kept\nin IX + 7 and replaced by the colour at $D6E8 + the cursor's kind (IX + 6). In a Timex mode\n($5C7F bit 3) the cursor is drawn as a character instead (CURSOR_XOR_CHAR).\nExit: carry.","comment":"B = the screen line"},
        "4383": {"comment":"A Timex mode?"},
        "4389": {"comment":"HL = its attribute"},
        "4392": {"comment":"Kept in IX + 7"},
        "4396": {"comment":"The colour for the cursor's kind"},
        "4399": {"comment":"The cursor colours from $D6E8"},
        "4405": {"comment":"The cursor's colour in"},
        "4408": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off line B of the window, column C: the attribute kept in IX + 7 put back;\nin a Timex mode the character is drawn again (CURSOR_XOR_CHAR), which takes it off.","comment":"B = the screen line"},
        "4411": {"comment":"A Timex mode?"},
        "4415": {"comment":"Draw the character again"},
        "4417": {"comment":"HL = the attribute address"},
        "4420": {"comment":"The attribute kept"},
        "4423": {"comment":"Put back"},
        "4425": {"synopsis":"Draws the cursor at line B, column C with OVER 1, so that drawing it twice takes it off: UDG\n= ROM 0's own pictures (UDG_ROM_GLYPHS), AT B, C (ROM 0's $07BA), OVER 1, the character $92\n+ the kind (IX + 6; ROM 0's CURSOR_CODE), OVER 0, and UDG back (UDG_SWAP).","comment":"ROM 0's UDG_ROM_GLYPHS: HL = the old UDG"},
        "4428": {"comment":"The old UDG kept"},
        "4429": {"comment":"ROM 0's $07BA: AT B, C"},
        "4432": {"comment":"OVER 1"},
        "4438": {"comment":"The cursor's picture, $92 + its kind"},
        "4441": {"comment":"ROM 0's CURSOR_CODE: A + $92"},
        "4444": {"comment":"The picture printed"},
        "4445": {"comment":"OVER 0"},
        "4450": {"comment":"ROM 0's UDG_SWAP: UDG back"},
        "4455": {"synopsis":"In a Timex mode ($5C7F bit 3): B + the window's top line (WIN_LINE_ADD); otherwise nothing.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4459": {"comment":"Not a Timex mode: B as it is"},
        "4460": {"synopsis":"B = B + IX + 1: line B of the window as a screen line.\nChanges: A."},
        "4463": {"comment":"B + the window's top line"},
        "4466": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E up by one (pixels and attributes, each line from the one\nbelow), then prints the row at HL on line E (SCROLL_PRINT)."},
        "4467": {"comment":"H = 0: up"},
        "4469": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "4471": {"comment":"On to the scroll"},
        "4473": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E down by one (B the upper; each line from the one above,\nstarting at E), then prints the row at HL on line B."},
        "4474": {"comment":"B and E swapped: start at E"},
        "4477": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "4478": {"comment":"H = $FF: down"},
        "4480": {"synopsis":"C = the lines to move; none when B = E."},
        "4481": {"comment":"Only one line?"},
        "4483": {"comment":"Just the row printed"},
        "4485": {"comment":"E kept: the line freed"},
        "4486": {"comment":"B = the line as ROM 3 counts lines"},
        "4489": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR), and the source's, one below (up)\nor one above (down)."},
        "4490": {"comment":"C = the direction"},
        "4491": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = line B"},
        "4494": {"comment":"DE = the line moved into"},
        "4495": {"comment":"Up or down?"},
        "4499": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "4502": {"synopsis":"Up: the line below."},
        "4503": {"synopsis":"Its 8 pixel rows copied, 32 bytes each, then its 32 attributes."},
        "4504": {"comment":"HL = the source line"},
        "4507": {"comment":"DE = the line moved into"},
        "4508": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "4509": {"comment":"32 bytes a pixel row"},
        "4511": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4513": {"comment":"A Timex mode: two display files"},
        "4519": {"comment":"Bank $0B at $6000 (ROM 0's MMU3_SWAP)"},
        "4522": {"comment":"A' = $0B"},
        "4526": {"synopsis":"One pixel row in both display files ($4000 and $6000)."},
        "4529": {"comment":"The second display file, $2000 on"},
        "4536": {"comment":"Back to the first display file"},
        "4540": {"comment":"The next pixel row down"},
        "4542": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4544": {"comment":"MMU 3 back; no attributes"},
        "4549": {"synopsis":"One pixel row."},
        "4552": {"comment":"The next pixel row down"},
        "4554": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "4556": {"comment":"The direction and DE kept"},
        "4558": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR for the line"},
        "4561": {"comment":"DE = the attributes moved into"},
        "4563": {"comment":"And for its source"},
        "4566": {"comment":"HL = the source's attributes"},
        "4569": {"comment":"The 32 attributes"},
        "4574": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "4575": {"synopsis":"The line done: B to the next, the way it goes."},
        "4576": {"comment":"Up or down?"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "4582": {"synopsis":"Up: the next line is the one below."},
        "4583": {"synopsis":"The next, while C counts."},
        "4584": {"comment":"H = the direction again"},
        "4587": {"comment":"B = the line left free"},
        "4589": {"synopsis":"The freed line printed: the row at HL on line B (PRINT_ROW)."},
        "4590": {"comment":"C = the line"},
        "4591": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL on window line C, from column 0, in its syntax colours (ROW_COLOURED):\nATTR_T and MASK_T set for it, P_FLAG's temporary bits cleared, TV_FLAG bit 0 = $D5B7 bit 6\n(editing in the lower screen) and AT C, 0 (ROM 0's $07BA; in a Timex mode the window's top\nline added). With $D741 bit 2 set (no screen output) the row is only scanned. TV_FLAG is put\nback. From $0217, $09F1, $0AC4 and $0AEE.\nExit: carry; A = the syntax state at the row's end, B = its bits for the next row\n(ROW_COLOURED).","comment":"TV_FLAG kept"},
        "4594": {"comment":"Kept, put back at the end"},
        "4595": {"comment":"Screen output off: A = 4, a scan only"},
        "4600": {"comment":"Off: only scanned"},
        "4604": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "4605": {"comment":"The lower screen ($D5B7 bit 6)?"},
        "4610": {"comment":"Main screen"},
        "4614": {"comment":"Lower screen"},
        "4616": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG with bit 0 for the screen part."},
        "4619": {"comment":"MASK_T = 0"},
        "4622": {"comment":"MASK_T = 0"},
        "4624": {"comment":"P_FLAG: the temporary bits cleared"},
        "4629": {"comment":"AT C, 0"},
        "4630": {"comment":"B = the line, column 0"},
        "4636": {"comment":"ROM 0's $07BA: AT B, C"},
        "4639": {"comment":"BC, HL back"},
        "4641": {"comment":"A = 0: printed"},
        "4642": {"synopsis":"The row printed or scanned; TV_FLAG back."},
        "4645": {"comment":"H = TV_FLAG; the row back on the stack"},
        "4646": {"comment":"L = the state"},
        "4647": {"comment":"TV_FLAG back"},
        "4651": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "4655": {"synopsis":"The syntax state at the end of the row at HL: ROW_COLOURED with A = 4, nothing printed."},
        "4657": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL (when A bit 2 is clear; A = 4 only scans it), each cell in the colour\nof its part of the BASIC line, set as ATTR_T from a table in bank 7. The state is the row's\nflags byte (C, from HL + ($D73D)): bit 0 a line number may come, bit 2 in a dot command, bit\n5 at a statement's start, bit 6 the rest is a comment, bit 7 inside quotes.\n1. 0: a space in colour $D6DA.\n2. Codes 1-$1F, a keyword's characters (LINE_TO_ROWS): 6-$1F as 'A'-'Z', 1, 2, 4, 5 as ' ',\n   '!', '#', '$', in colour $D6EE; 3 is the R of REM and starts a comment.\n3. Digits at a line's start: colour $D6ED (the line number).\n4. At a statement's start '.' starts a dot command (colour $D6F5 up to ':') and ';' a\n   comment.\n5. Otherwise: a comment $D6F1, quotes and the text in them $D6F0, a letter $D6F2, a digit\n   $D6F3, anything else $D6F4; ':' starts a statement.\n6. Codes $80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN.\nExit: A = the state (bit 0 cleared), B = its bits 2, 5, 6 and 7 for a next row. Keeps HL,\nDE, C.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "4660": {"comment":"D = the mode"},
        "4661": {"comment":"B = the columns"},
        "4665": {"comment":"C = the row's flags, the state"},
        "4668": {"comment":"HL = the row again"},
        "4670": {"synopsis":"One cell: a space?"},
        "4672": {"comment":"A space: classed with the text"},
        "4676": {"comment":"Below a space: a code"},
        "4678": {"comment":"A line number may come?"},
        "4680": {"comment":"No: the line number is over"},
        "4682": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "4685": {"comment":"Not a digit: the line number is over"},
        "4687": {"comment":"Statement start after it; colour $D6ED"},
        "4694": {"synopsis":"An empty cell: a space in colour $D6DA."},
        "4696": {"comment":"Colour $D6DA, normal"},
        "4701": {"synopsis":"Codes 1-$1F: a keyword's characters."},
        "4702": {"comment":"0: an empty cell"},
        "4704": {"comment":"No line number, no statement start now"},
        "4708": {"comment":"6-$1F: 'A'-'Z'"},
        "4710": {"comment":"6 or more?"},
        "4714": {"comment":"1-5: ' ', '!', 'R', '#', '$'"},
        "4716": {"comment":"3?"},
        "4720": {"comment":"3: REM's R, a comment follows"},
        "4724": {"synopsis":"In colour $D6EE, unless in a comment."},
        "4728": {"comment":"Keyword colour $D6EE"},
        "4733": {"synopsis":"A character from '!' up: the line number over."},
        "4735": {"comment":"At a statement's start?"},
        "4739": {"comment":"'.': a dot command"},
        "4743": {"comment":"'.': bit 2 kept, on"},
        "4745": {"comment":"Not a dot command"},
        "4747": {"comment":"';': a comment"},
        "4749": {"comment":"Not ';'"},
        "4753": {"synopsis":"Codes $80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN."},
        "4755": {"comment":"$80 up: ROW_COL_TOKEN"},
        "4757": {"synopsis":"The statement started."},
        "4759": {"synopsis":"The colour by the state, then by the character.","comment":"A comment?"},
        "4761": {"comment":"Comment colour"},
        "4766": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "4768": {"comment":"String colour"},
        "4773": {"comment":"A quote itself: as a string"},
        "4775": {"comment":"A quote: string colour"},
        "4777": {"comment":"A dot command?"},
        "4779": {"comment":"Dot command colour"},
        "4782": {"comment":"In a dot command: ':' ends it"},
        "4784": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "4787": {"comment":"Letter colour"},
        "4792": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "4795": {"comment":"Digit colour"},
        "4800": {"comment":"Anything else"},
        "4803": {"synopsis":"':' starts a statement; a dot command ends.","comment":"':'?"},
        "4807": {"comment":"A statement starts; no dot command"},
        "4811": {"synopsis":"ATTR_T = the colour at DE; printed unless only scanning."},
        "4812": {"comment":"The colour from the table"},
        "4816": {"comment":"A = the character, D = the mode"},
        "4818": {"comment":"Printing?"},
        "4820": {"comment":"RST $28: printed"},
        "4823": {"synopsis":"A quote flips the in-quotes bit.","comment":"The cell's own character: a quote?"},
        "4828": {"comment":"The in-quotes bit flipped"},
        "4832": {"synopsis":"The next cell, up to the last column."},
        "4834": {"comment":"The next cell"},
        "4837": {"comment":"The state at the row's end"},
        "4840": {"comment":"HL, DE, BC back"},
        "4843": {"comment":"B = the bits a next row starts with"},
        "4847": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "4849": {"synopsis":"Codes $80 up: $80-$8F printed as they are; $90-$A9 as 'A'-'Z', $AA-$B1 as '1'-'8', $B2-$CB\nas 'a'-'z', $CC-$E5 as 'a'-'z' and $E6-$FF as 'A'-'Z' underlined (OVER 1, a backspace and\n'_'). In the standard mode ($5C7F bits 0-3 clear) they take colour $D6EF; codes $90 up are\nshown INVERSE 1 when that colour is $D6DA's, and always in the other modes."},
        "4850": {"comment":"Only scanning?"},
        "4852": {"comment":"Only scanning: no print"},
        "4854": {"comment":"The code kept"},
        "4855": {"comment":"The standard screen mode?"},
        "4860": {"comment":"Another mode: INVERSE for $90 up"},
        "4862": {"comment":"The normal colour"},
        "4866": {"comment":"And $D6EF, ATTR_T now"},
        "4872": {"comment":"Not the same: no inverse"},
        "4873": {"comment":"Different colours: no inverse"},
        "4875": {"synopsis":"Codes $90 up: INVERSE 1."},
        "4877": {"comment":"Codes $90 up?"},
        "4881": {"comment":"INVERSE 1"},
        "4887": {"synopsis":"The code turned into a character; E = 2 to underline it."},
        "4888": {"comment":"E = 1: not underlined"},
        "4890": {"comment":"$80-$8F as they are"},
        "4894": {"comment":"$90-$A9: 'A'-'Z'"},
        "4896": {"comment":"Below $AA?"},
        "4900": {"comment":"$AA up: E = 2"},
        "4901": {"comment":"$E6-$FF: 'A'-'Z', underlined"},
        "4903": {"comment":"$E6 up?"},
        "4907": {"comment":"$CC-$E5: 'a'-'z', underlined"},
        "4909": {"comment":"$CC up?"},
        "4913": {"comment":"$B2-$CB: 'a'-'z', not underlined"},
        "4916": {"comment":"$B2 up?"},
        "4920": {"comment":"$AA-$B1: '1'-'8'"},
        "4922": {"synopsis":"Printed, then INVERSE 0; when underlining, OVER 1, a backspace, '_', OVER 0."},
        "4923": {"comment":"INVERSE 0"},
        "4928": {"comment":"Underline?"},
        "4929": {"comment":"No underline: the next cell"},
        "4931": {"comment":"OVER 1"},
        "4934": {"comment":"E = 1"},
        "4936": {"comment":"Back over it, an underline"},
        "4939": {"comment":"'_'"},
        "4942": {"comment":"OVER 0"},
        "4947": {"comment":"The next cell"},
        "4949": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a digit '0'-'9'.\nChanges: F."},
        "4951": {"comment":"Above '9': no carry"},
        "4952": {"comment":"Below '0': no carry"},
        "4956": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter, A-Z or a-z.\nChanges: F."},
        "4959": {"comment":"Below 'A': no carry"},
        "4960": {"comment":"Below '[': carry"},
        "4963": {"comment":"Below 'a': no carry"},
        "4967": {"comment":"Below '{': carry"},
        "4970": {"synopsis":"Clears the window's screen lines, from its top line (IX + 1) to that + ($D73C), through ROM\n0's CLEAR_LINES. From $0337.\nChanges: as that routine."},
        "4973": {"comment":"C = the window's last line"},
        "4976": {"comment":"Plus the top line"},
        "4978": {"comment":"ROM 0's CLEAR_LINES: lines B to C"},
        "4982": {"synopsis":"B = 24 - B - (IX + 1): line B of the window as ROM 3 counts lines.\nChanges: A, B."},
        "4984": {"comment":"24 - B"},
        "4985": {"comment":"Less the window's top line"},
        "4990": {"synopsis":"HL = $5800 + 32 x B + C, the attribute address of line B, column C. Keeps BC.\nChanges: A, DE, HL."},
        "4991": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "4992": {"comment":"DE = 32 x B"},
        "4994": {"comment":"Three right shifts of B:E"},
        "5006": {"comment":"The attribute area"},
        "5009": {"comment":"Plus C"},
        "5010": {"comment":"Plus 32 x B"},
        "5014": {"synopsis":"Copies C bytes from HL to DE (LDIR, B = 0). Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, HL, DE kept"},
        "5017": {"comment":"BC = C"},
        "5021": {"comment":"All back"},
        "5025": {"synopsis":"Steps the editor's column count ($D73D) round COLUMN_CYCLE, 32 to 64 to 85 to 32\n(SET_COLUMNS), applies it (ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY) and restarts the editor (EDITOR_RESTART).\nNo reference to it was found in either page or in NextZXOS.","comment":"The column count now"},
        "5031": {"synopsis":"Up to the count now in the table."},
        "5035": {"comment":"L = the next count"},
        "5039": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY, then EDITOR_RESTART."},
        "5042": {"synopsis":"Restarts the editor with the mode in $D5EC: START_KEEP_EPPC ($0303), which stores it in\n$D5B8 and $D5EC, sets $D74E = E_PPC and clears bank 7 from $C000 (the row buffers) on."},
        "5045": {"synopsis":"$0303 with the mode in A (from MODE_TOGGLE)."},
        "5048": {"synopsis":"Moves the editor between the main and the lower screen: $D5B8 = 0, the columns applied (ROM\n0's COLUMNS_APPLY), the font set ($03BD), $D5B7 bit 6 flipped and bit 3 cleared; bit 6 set:\nthe lower screen ($041D); clear: the main screen ($042F, COLUMNS_APPLY again). The line in\n$D74E is set up (PREV_LINE_NUM) and the editor shown ($010C). From $0417 and NextZXOS ROM\n0's MENU_SCREEN ($11DA). Keeps IX.\nExit: carry."},
        "5050": {"comment":"The state byte $D5B8 = 0"},
        "5051": {"comment":"$D5B8 = 0"},
        "5054": {"comment":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY"},
        "5057": {"comment":"The font for the column count"},
        "5060": {"comment":"The lower screen flipped"},
        "5063": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped, bit 3 cleared"},
        "5069": {"comment":"Now the lower screen?"},
        "5073": {"comment":"To the lower screen"},
        "5076": {"comment":"On to the line"},
        "5078": {"synopsis":"To the main screen."},
        "5081": {"comment":"ROM 0's COLUMNS_APPLY"},
        "5087": {"comment":"A line kept?"},
        "5092": {"comment":"The editor shown ($010C)"},
        "5095": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "5099": {"synopsis":"Sets the editor's column count: $D73D = L (H = 0) and $D73F = L + 3, the length of a row\n(its cells, a flags byte and a line number). From COLUMNS_NEXT and NextZXOS ROM 1's A3C_SET\n($0216, L = 32, 64 or 85).\nChanges: HL.","comment":"H = 0"},
        "5101": {"comment":"The column count"},
        "5104": {"comment":"The cells, flags and a number"},
        "5107": {"comment":"The row length"},
        "5111": {"synopsis":"COLUMNS_NEXT's table: each count followed by the next: 32, 64, 85, 32."},
        "5115": {"synopsis":"Restarts the editor (EDITOR_RESTART_A) in mode 8 when $D5EC is 0, otherwise in mode 0. No\nreference to it was found in either page or in NextZXOS."},
        "5119": {"comment":"8 when $D5EC = 0"},
        "5123": {"comment":"Otherwise mode 0"},
        "5126": {"synopsis":"With bank 0: NextZXOS ROM 1's CALL_DMMC_27A8 (the DivMMC memory's $27A8 with BC = HL = 10);\nbank 7; with no carry a beep ($03B9); E_PPC = 0; then COLUMNS_RESTART. No reference to it\nwas found in either page or in NextZXOS."},
        "5127": {"comment":"ROM 1's CALL_DMMC_27A8"},
        "5130": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5131": {"comment":"No carry: a beep"},
        "5134": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "5137": {"comment":"E_PPC, the current line"},
        "5142": {"synopsis":"The alternate stack ($5B6A) moved to UDG - 1; with bank 0, NextZXOS ROM 1's CLEAR_CHECK\n($3485); bank 7; then COLUMNS_RESTART. No reference to it was found in either page or in\nNextZXOS.","comment":"UDG - 1"},
        "5147": {"comment":"The alternate stack's top"},
        "5151": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "5152": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLEAR_CHECK"},
        "5161": {"synopsis":"Key $11 (EDIT_KEY_TABLE; NextZXOS ROM 0's LINEIN_KEY_11 at $2A70 too): FLAGS2 ($5C6A) bit 7\nflipped.\nExit: A = 0, carry.","comment":"FLAGS2"},
        "5164": {"synopsis":"Flips bit 7 of (HL).\nExit: A = 0, carry.","comment":"Bit 7"},
        "5168": {"comment":"A = 0, carry"},
        "5171": {"synopsis":"Key $12 (EDIT_KEY_TABLE): TV_FLAG bit 7 flipped (with it set, EXPAND_NEXT expands keywords\ninside quotes too), then EDITOR_RESTART.","comment":"TV_FLAG"},
        "5174": {"comment":"Bit 7 flipped"},
        "5180": {"synopsis":"The editor's key table, read by $039F (through $00E4): for each key a code and the address\nof its routine (a word), ended by $FF: $0B $05E4, $0A $0605, $08 $0627, $09 $0633, $0C\n$049B, $0D $04C2, $1F $05A0, $1E $0576, $04 $052A, $05 $0535, $1A $04FE, $01 $0525, $1D\n$05D7, $00 $05CA, $18 $0488, $1C $0BBE, $1B $0B5F, $10 $0C16, $03 $0BE4, $11 KEY_11, $12\nKEY_12, $19 $040F, $07 $03F7."},
        "5250": {"synopsis":"PREV_LINE_START for the line before line HL.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone. From NextZXOS ROM 1's STORE_LINE_NEW ($0D6D) too."},
        "5253": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5254": {"comment":"None: HL = 0, no carry"},
        "5258": {"synopsis":"NEXT_LINE_START for the line after line HL (the first line for HL = 0).\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone."},
        "5261": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5262": {"comment":"None: HL = 0, no carry"},
        "5326": {"comment":"Its next character"},
        "5327": {"comment":"HL = the next one"},
