        "5417": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "5418": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 7 clear and inside quotes: the byte as it is.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 7: keywords in quotes too"},
        "5424": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "5426": {"comment":"Yes: the byte as it is"},
        "5443": {"comment":"Its text given now"},
        "5447": {"comment":"Below $81: a character"},
        "5522": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5524": {"comment":"The ROM back in MMU 1"},
        "5528": {"comment":"At the 8K page's end?"},
        "5537": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5539": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; HL = the offset; carry."},
        "5540": {"comment":"The offset in the bank"},
        "5544": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE in mode 1 ($D7EE = 1), from $085E: the line is walked, not written, to find X_PTR's\nplace in the text.","comment":"Mode 1: walked"},
        "5548": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE in mode 0 ($D7EE = 0), from $0817: the line is written.","comment":"Mode 0: written"},
        "5550": {"synopsis":"Turns the line the editor holds, read character by character (TOK_GET_CHAR), into a BASIC\nline at E_LINE:\n1. The work space cleared with bank 0: ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS (A = 0) or CLEAR_WS (A not 0),\n   through ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC.\n2. $D7EE = D (the mode), $D7EC = SP, $D7F7 = A (where the characters come from: 0 the\n   editor's rows, 1 the banked buffer of IDE_TOKENISER, $FF memory), $D7EA = E_LINE (the\n   place written), $D7EF-$D7F5 cleared; the RAM routines copied (RAM_ROUTINES).\n3. Each character goes through a small state machine in $D7F1: letters, '#' and '$' are\n   collected into a word at $D7E1 (TOK_BUF_ADD), which a following character looks up as a\n   keyword (KEYWORD_LOOKUP); a word that is not one is written as text (TOK_FLUSH), one that\n   holds a space is split there (TOK_SPLIT).\n4. Characters are written by TOK_OUT; ENTER ends the line.\nExit: no carry at the end of the line (mode 0); in mode 1, reaching X_PTR returns from here\nwith carry and BC = the characters before it (TOK_WRITE). Bank 7.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5551": {"synopsis":"TOKENIZE with A on entry: 0 or not 0 as above.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "5557": {"comment":"A = 0: ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS instead"},
        "5560": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; ROM 3's routine at BC (ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC); bank 7."},
        "5561": {"comment":"ROM 0's ROM3_CALL_BC"},
        "5564": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "5565": {"comment":"B = the mode"},
        "5566": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "5585": {"comment":"7 bytes: $D7EF-$D7F5"},
        "5592": {"comment":"The RAM routines to $D772"},
        "5601": {"comment":"In a word?"},
        "5603": {"comment":"State 1"},
        "5605": {"comment":"Another state: written as it is"},
        "5606": {"comment":"Not state 0"},
        "5608": {"synopsis":"State 0: a letter?"},
        "5610": {"comment":"Not a letter: written"},
        "5612": {"synopsis":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD): state 1."},
        "5615": {"comment":"Full"},
        "5617": {"comment":"State 1: in a word"},
        "5622": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5624": {"synopsis":"The buffer full: split at a space (TOK_SPLIT), or written as text (TOK_FLUSH) and the rest\nof the word passed ($D7F1 bit 4)."},
        "5627": {"comment":"Split: on with the character"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Bit 4: the rest of the word as text"},
        "5634": {"comment":"On with the character"},
        "5636": {"synopsis":"B written (TOK_OUT); a character other than a letter ends a passed word. At ENTER in mode 0,\nTOKENIZE ends with no carry.","comment":"A letter?"},
        "5638": {"comment":"No: the word passing ends"},
        "5645": {"comment":"The line's end: no carry"},
        "5646": {"comment":"The next character"},
