        "7016": {"synopsis":"A note, with its length before it: no digit, the current length; 1-9 a length (it becomes\nthe current one), 10-12 a triplet (three notes of the length); '_' ties more lengths to it.\nThe lengths go into the block's list, the count at IX + 33; then PLAY_NEXT returns. A length\nof 0 or over 12 is report n; more than 10 lengths report o.","comment":"A digit?"},
        "7021": {"comment":"HL = the block's length list"},
        "7024": {"comment":"The string's pointer to it = HL"},
        "7027": {"comment":"No lengths yet"},
        "7031": {"comment":"Back to the digit"},
        "7034": {"comment":"BC = the length's number"},
        "7037": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "7038": {"comment":"0?"},
        "7039": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "7042": {"comment":"Over 12?"},
        "7044": {"comment":"Report n"},
        "7047": {"comment":"1-9?"},
