        "8323": {"comment":"Wait while SPACE is down"},
        "8325": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key yet"},
        "8381": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8384": {"comment":"'-' given ($5B66 bit 7)?"},
        "8388": {"comment":"No: the long name"},
        "8390": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8392": {"comment":"8 name letters"},
        "8394": {"synopsis":"One name letter, without its attribute bit.","comment":"A letter, its attribute bit off"},
        "8398": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8401": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8403": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "8408": {"comment":"3 type letters"},
        "8410": {"synopsis":"One type letter, without its attribute bit.","comment":"A letter, its attribute bit off"},
        "8414": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8417": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8427": {"synopsis":"TAB 25, then the attributes as text (ROM 0's MAKE_ATTR_TEXT); with EXP: they, the date and\ntime, and the size in bytes (or nothing for a directory).","comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8430": {"comment":"TAB 25 and a space ($245C)"},
        "8436": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8439": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8440": {"comment":"+ 7: its attribute letters"},
        "8444": {"comment":"The attributes as text at $5B9D; B bit 0: a directory (ROM 0)"},
        "8506": {"synopsis":"The size in K (NextZXOS ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5, spaces before) and \"K\".","comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8521": {"comment":"\"K\""},
        "8526": {"synopsis":"ENTER; the next entry.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8531": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8534": {"comment":"HL = the size's address"},
        "8535": {"comment":"+ 2: the next entry"},
        "8537": {"comment":"A = the names left"},
        "8538": {"comment":"One less"},
        "8539": {"comment":"More?"},
        "8542": {"comment":"B = the entries DOS_CATALOG gave"},
        "8543": {"comment":"63: the buffer was full, more may follow"},
        "8546": {"comment":"No: the end"},
        "8548": {"comment":"The last entry (63, at $FA33)"},
        "8551": {"comment":"To entry 0: the next call goes on from it"},
        "8559": {"comment":"HL = $F70B, its size"},
        "8560": {"comment":"$FA there: not 0, more were found"},
        "8561": {"comment":"The next part"},
        "8564": {"synopsis":"ENTER after the last entry.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8567": {"synopsis":"The sort's memory freed ($272D: DOS_CATALOG with B = 2, C = $20, A = 0); the free space on\nthe drive given, or on the default one (DOS_SET_DRIVE), printed with \" free\" ($240B, $246F).","comment":"The sort's memory freed ($272D)"},
        "8570": {"comment":"A drive letter given?"},
        "8574": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8576": {"comment":"A = $FF: ask"},
        "8578": {"comment":"The default drive (DOS_SET_DRIVE, ROM 2)"},
        "8581": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8584": {"synopsis":"DOS_FREE_SPACE (ROM 2) for drive A.","comment":"The free space on drive A (DOS_FREE_SPACE, ROM 2)"},
        "8587": {"comment":"An error"},
        "8590": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8593": {"comment":"Printed in K, M or G ($240B)"},
        "8596": {"comment":"\" free\" and ENTER"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"Nothing matched: \"No files found\" ($2475) unless an earlier part of the catalogue was\nprinted (entry 0's size byte, $F70B, not 0); then CAT_FREE.","comment":"Did any part come before (entry 0's size byte not 0)?"},
        "8606": {"comment":"\"No files found\""},
        "8609": {"comment":"RAM bank 0"},
        "8612": {"comment":"Only when nothing came before"},
        "8615": {"comment":"RAM bank 7"},
        "8618": {"comment":"The free space"},
        "8620": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A of ROM 3's keyword table (ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN, 0 = RND) with FLAGS bit 0\nset first, so no space goes before it. Called with $25 (LINE), $3F (DATA) and $0A (CODE) by\nTAPE_CAT.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL (what PRINT_TOKEN changes).","comment":"FLAGS bit 0: no space before the keyword"},
        "8624": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_TOKEN"},
        "8628": {"synopsis":"CAT ASN (CAT followed by the token ASN, from $1F82): past ASN; checking ends at the\nstatement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each drive letter A-P ROM 2's\nIDE_DOS_MAPPING ($00F7) with L = $80 + the letter (the 256-byte form, BC = $D827): a mapped\ndrive prints as the letter, \": \" and the description ROM 2 left at $D827 ($FF-ended, ROM 1's\nPRINT_MSG), then ENTER. An error from ROM 2 goes to $2046. Ends in bank 0.","comment":"Past ASN"},
        "8629": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8635": {"comment":"16 drive letters"},
        "8637": {"comment":"From 'A'"},
        "8639": {"synopsis":"One letter: L = 'A'-'P', B the letters left.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8640": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "8654": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "8656": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8660": {"comment":"':'"},
        "8684": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8688": {"synopsis":"CAT TAB (CAT followed by the token TAB, from $1F87): lists the cards' partitions. Past TAB;\nchecking ends at the statement's end ($0149). Running, in bank 7, for each of 16 units:\n1. ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY ($01B4, C = the unit): a unit that fails is skipped (CAT_TAB_FREE).\n2. In bank 0: ENTER, \"Unit \", its number, \": \"; 16 bytes copied from IX (left by\n   IDE_CAPACITY) into 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) by ROM 2's $05CC and\n   printed; \", \" and the capacity (PRINT_SECTORS_A, no padding), ENTER.\n3. Every partition entry from 0 (CAT_TAB_ENTRY); unused ones counted; then the count and \"\n   free partition entries\" (CAT_TAB_FREE).\nEnds in bank 0.","comment":"Past TAB"},
        "8689": {"comment":"The statement's end: checking stops here"},
        "8692": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8695": {"comment":"16 units"},
        "8697": {"synopsis":"One unit: A = 16 - B, the unit number; the free-entry count 0 kept on the stack under it.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "8698": {"comment":"A = 16 - B, the unit number"},
        "8701": {"comment":"The free-entry count, 0"},
        "8705": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8706": {"comment":"C = the unit"},
        "8707": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_CAPACITY: DEHL = its sectors"},
        "8710": {"comment":"No such unit: on to the next"},
        "8713": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "8715": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8718": {"comment":"The capacity kept (DEHL)"},
        "8720": {"comment":"The unit kept"},
        "8721": {"comment":"ENTER, \"Unit \""},
        "8727": {"comment":"The unit number"},
        "8728": {"comment":"HL = the unit"},
        "8731": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "8736": {"comment":"\": \""},
        "8742": {"comment":"17 bytes of workspace"},
        "8745": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8748": {"comment":"HL = IX, as IDE_CAPACITY left it"},
        "8751": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "8752": {"comment":"16 bytes"},
        "8755": {"comment":"ROM 2's $05CC (the DivMMC memory's copy routine)"},
        "8758": {"comment":"A = $A0 (PRINT_TEXT_DE does not read it)"},
        "8760": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "8761": {"comment":"Its text printed, up to a byte with bit 7 set"},
        "8764": {"comment":"\", \""},
        "8770": {"comment":"DEHL = the capacity again"},
        "8772": {"comment":"No padding"},
        "8774": {"comment":"The capacity, with its unit letter"},
        "8777": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8782": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8785": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "8788": {"synopsis":"Entry BC of the unit's partition table read into $F752 (ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, $00C4, A\n= the unit); an error goes to CAT_TAB_ERROR. Type 0 (the byte at $F762) is counted as free.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "8790": {"comment":"The entry's buffer"},
        "8793": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_PARTITON_READ, entry BC"},
        "8796": {"comment":"An error: CAT_TAB_ERROR"},
        "8799": {"comment":"The entry's type"},
        "8802": {"comment":"0: an unused entry?"},
        "8813": {"synopsis":"A partition: \"u>\" (the unit's number, '>'), its 16-character name from $F752 with $00 shown\nas '~'; a space, its size (the 32-bit word at $F769 + 1, in 512-byte sectors,\nPRINT_SECTORS), a space and its type's name from PART_TYPE_NAMES; ENTER.","comment":"The unit"},
        "8821": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8827": {"comment":"'>' after the unit"},
        "8832": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8835": {"comment":"The name"},
        "8838": {"comment":"16 characters"},
        "8840": {"synopsis":"One character of the name.","comment":"One character"},
        "8842": {"comment":"$00?"},
        "8845": {"comment":"Shown as '~'"},
        "8847": {"synopsis":"Printed; E counts the 16.","comment":"Printed in bank 0"},
        "8850": {"comment":"The next of the 16"},
        "8853": {"comment":"The type"},
        "8856": {"comment":"Plus 3: its name's number in the table"},
        "8859": {"comment":"DEHL = the 32-bit word at $F769"},
        "8866": {"comment":"plus 1: the size in sectors"},
        "8872": {"synopsis":"The size and the spaces round it, in bank 0; C = the type + 3, the type name's number in\nPART_TYPE_NAMES.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8875": {"comment":"The name's number kept"},
        "8876": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8881": {"comment":"The size, blanks before it"},
        "8884": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8889": {"comment":"C back"},
        "8890": {"comment":"The table of type names"},
        "8893": {"comment":"20 names at most"},
        "8895": {"synopsis":"Names skipped until C reaches 1 (20 at most).","comment":"Down to this name?"},
        "8898": {"synopsis":"One name's bytes, up to the one with bit 7 set.","comment":"The bytes of a name"},
        "8900": {"comment":"Bit 7 into the carry: the last?"},
        "8903": {"comment":"The next name"},
        "8905": {"synopsis":"The type's name printed (PRINT_TEXT_DE at $013D), ENTER; bank 7 again.","comment":"The type's name printed"},
        "8908": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "8913": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "8916": {"comment":"The entry number back"},
        "8917": {"synopsis":"The next entry, until BC wraps round to 0.","comment":"The next entry"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Until BC wraps round to 0"},
        "8923": {"synopsis":"The end of the unit's table: a free-entry count that is not 0 is printed with \" free\npartition entries\" and two ENTERs (MSG_FREE_ENTRIES).","comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8924": {"comment":"HL = the free-entry count"},
        "8925": {"comment":"None?"},
        "8947": {"comment":"The next unit"},
        "8951": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "8955": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ failed: error $38 is the table's end (CAT_TAB_FREE); $16 ends the unit\nwith no count; any other is reported ($2046).","comment":"Error $38: the end of the table"},
        "8959": {"comment":"Error $16: the unit has no table"},
        "8961": {"comment":"Others are reported"},
        "8964": {"comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "8965": {"comment":"Drop the count"},
        "8966": {"comment":"The next unit, with no count"},
        "8968": {"synopsis":"CAT of the tape (from $1FF9, for a name of two characters starting 'T:'): lists the headers\non the tape until BREAK. 17 bytes of workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) hold each header, IX at\nthem.\nThe same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT.","comment":"17 bytes for a header"},
        "8971": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM: DE = the room"},
        "8974": {"comment":"IX = the room"},
        "8977": {"synopsis":"A new line, then the next header (the same job as the +3E's TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "8982": {"synopsis":"BREAK (SPACE, port $7FFE bit 0, and CAPS SHIFT, port $FEFE bit 0, both down) ends the list.","comment":"Port $7FFE: SPACE"},
        "8986": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "8987": {"comment":"SPACE not pressed: go on"},
        "8989": {"comment":"Port $FEFE: CAPS SHIFT"},
        "8993": {"comment":"Bit 0 into the carry"},
        "8994": {"comment":"Not pressed: go on"},
        "8996": {"comment":"BREAK: done"},
        "8997": {"synopsis":"A header from the tape: flag 0, 17 bytes, loading (ROM 3's LD_BYTES); a failure tries again.\nThen the name in quotes and a space, and by the type: 0 \"BASIC \" and LINE n when it has a\nstart line; 1 and 2 TAPE_CAT_ARRAY; 3 TAPE_CAT_CODE; higher TAPE_CAT_LAYER.","comment":"The flag byte: a header"},
        "8999": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "9002": {"comment":"Carry: load"},
        "9003": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9005": {"comment":"ROM 3's LD_BYTES"},
        "9008": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9010": {"comment":"Failed: try again"},
        "9012": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9014": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9019": {"comment":"10 characters of name"},
        "9021": {"synopsis":"One character of the name (header bytes 1-10).","comment":"One character"},
        "9027": {"comment":"On to the next"},
        "9029": {"comment":"For 10"},
        "9031": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9033": {"comment":"'\"'"},
        "9038": {"comment":"A space"},
        "9043": {"comment":"The type, header byte 0"},
        "9046": {"comment":"0, a program?"},
        "9050": {"comment":"\"BASIC \""},
        "9056": {"comment":"Header byte 14 bit 7: no start line?"},
        "9060": {"comment":"None: the next header"},
        "9062": {"comment":"LINE"},
        "9067": {"comment":"HL = the start line, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9073": {"comment":"No blanks before it"},
        "9080": {"synopsis":"Types 1 and 2, arrays: DATA, the array's letter (header byte 14, bit 7 off and bit 6 on),\nthen \"$() \" for type 2 or \"() \" for type 1 (MSG_ARRAY or one byte on).","comment":"Below 3: an array?"},
        "9082": {"comment":"No: CODE or higher"},
        "9084": {"comment":"The type kept"},
        "9085": {"comment":"DATA"},
        "9090": {"comment":"The array's name, header byte 14"},
        "9093": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "9095": {"comment":"Bit 6 on: a letter"},
        "9097": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9100": {"comment":"\"$() \""},
        "9103": {"comment":"The type back"},
        "9104": {"comment":"2, a string array?"},
        "9106": {"comment":"Yes: \"$() \""},
        "9108": {"comment":"No: \"() \""},
        "9109": {"synopsis":"The suffix printed.","comment":"Printed"},
        "9112": {"synopsis":"The next header (TAPE_CAT_NEXT).","comment":"The next header"},
        "9117": {"comment":"CODE"},
        "9122": {"comment":"HL = the start, header bytes 13-14"},
        "9133": {"comment":"','"},
        "9138": {"comment":"HL = the length, header bytes 11-12"},
        "9156": {"synopsis":"Prints a count of K: the size from ROM 2 in BCDE (K) doubled into DEHL, 512-byte sectors;\nthen PRINT_SECTORS. Called after DOS_FREE_SPACE (CAT_FREE_DRIVE) and by COPY_DATA with the K\ncopied so far.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = DE, the low word of BCDE"},
        "9157": {"comment":"Doubled: K into 512-byte sectors"},
        "9158": {"comment":"The carry into C and B"},
        "9162": {"comment":"DEHL = the sectors"},
        "9164": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL (in 512-byte sectors) with blanks before it (A = $20), as\nPRINT_SECTORS_A.","comment":"Blanks before the number"},
        "9166": {"synopsis":"Prints the size DEHL, in 512-byte sectors, as a number and a unit letter: DE = 0 gives K\n(DEHL / 2), D = 0 M (DEHL / 2048), otherwise G (DEHL / 2^21), the quotient rounded up when\nbits are lost. The number goes through ROM 1's NUM_OUT_5 with E = A ($20 blanks before it,\n$FF none), the letter through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nEntry: A = the padding character for NUM_OUT_5.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The padding kept"},
        "9167": {"comment":"1 shift, 'K'"},
        "9170": {"comment":"DE = 0?"},
        "9172": {"comment":"Yes: K"},
        "9174": {"comment":"11 shifts, 'M'"},
        "9177": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "9179": {"comment":"Yes: M"},
        "9181": {"comment":"21 shifts, 'G'"},
        "9184": {"synopsis":"B = the shift count, C = the letter: the bits shifted out are ORed into A.","comment":"A collects the bits shifted out"},
        "9185": {"synopsis":"One shift of DEHL to the right.","comment":"DEHL one bit right"},
        "9193": {"comment":"The bit out into A"},
        "9195": {"comment":"B times"},
        "9197": {"comment":"Any bits lost?"},
        "9198": {"comment":"No"},
        "9200": {"comment":"Yes: rounded up"},
        "9201": {"synopsis":"E = the padding; the number printed, then the letter.","comment":"The padding back"},
        "9202": {"comment":"E = the padding for NUM_OUT_5"},
        "9203": {"comment":"The letter kept"},
        "9207": {"comment":"The letter back"},
        "9208": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "9213": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER (PRINT_A_BANK0).","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9215": {"synopsis":"Prints A through ROM 3's PRINT_A with RAM bank 0 paged in ($00E8), then bank 7 again\n($00FF).\nChanges: AF (what PRINT_A changes).","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9218": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9221": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9225": {"synopsis":"CAT's column move, bit 7 on its last byte: TAB ($17) to column 25 ($19, $00), then a space.\nPrinted by PRINT_TEXT_DE ($013D) from CAT_ENTRY_ATTRS."},
        "9229": {"synopsis":"\"BASIC \", bit 7 on the last byte (TAPE_CAT)."},
        "9235": {"synopsis":"\"$() \", bit 7 on the last byte; TAPE_CAT prints it for a string array and from $2467, \"() \",\nfor a number array."},
        "9239": {"synopsis":"\"<DIR>\", bit 7 on the last byte (CAT_NO_EXP)."},
        "9244": {"synopsis":"\" free\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_FREE_DRIVE)."},
        "9250": {"synopsis":"\"No files found\" and ENTER, bit 7 on the ENTER (CAT_NO_FILES)."},
        "9265": {"synopsis":"ENTER and \"Unit \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9271": {"synopsis":"\": \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9273": {"synopsis":"\", \", bit 7 on the space (CAT_TAB)."},
        "9275": {"synopsis":"The partition types' names for CAT_TAB_TYPE, each ended by bit 7, number n for type n - 3:\n\"*BAD*\" ($FE), \"FREE\" ($FF), none (0), \"sys\" (1), \"swap\" (2), \"data\" (3), none (4-15, twelve\n$80s), \"FAT16\" ($10), \"FAT32\" ($11), none ($12)."},
        "9319": {"synopsis":"\" free partition entries\" and two ENTERs, bit 7 on the last (CAT_TAB_FREE)."},
        "9358": {"synopsis":"COPY \"name\" TO SCREEN$ or TO LPRINT (the syntax table's word at $048F): stream 3 when the\nsub-keyword kept at $5B5E is LPRINT ($E0), stream 2 otherwise; then COPY_STRM_SET.","comment":"The sub-keyword taken"},
        "9363": {"comment":"Stream 3, the printer"},
        "9367": {"comment":"No: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "9405": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9411": {"comment":"Open action 1, create action 0: it must exist"},
        "9414": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9419": {"comment":"No byte before the first"},
        "9421": {"synopsis":"The next byte: D = the last one.","comment":"D = the last byte"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Kept over the call"},
        "9423": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9425": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_BYTE_READ: C = the byte"},
        "9428": {"comment":"D back"},
        "9429": {"comment":"A byte read?"},
        "9431": {"comment":"No: $19, the file's end?"},
        "9433": {"comment":"Another error: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9567": {"comment":"One file copied"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Then the count"},
        "9573": {"synopsis":"A ROM 2 call failed, or COPY found an error, error code in A: files 2, 1 and 0 closed (ROM\n2's DOS_CLOSE, $0109), each one that will not close abandoned (DOS_ABANDON, $010C); ENTER.\nWith $D7FD bit 7 set (DOS_FAIL_QUIET) SP goes back to $D5D6's value and NC returns the error\nto COPY_TO_FILE_GO's caller; otherwise ROM 1's DOS_ERROR_BANK0 reports it.\nThe same job as the +3E's DOS_FAIL.","comment":"The error kept"},
        "9574": {"comment":"Files 2, 1 and 0"},
        "9576": {"synopsis":"One file: B = 2, 1, 0.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9577": {"comment":"B = the file"},
        "9579": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9582": {"comment":"B back"},
        "9583": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "9585": {"comment":"No: ROM 2's DOS_ABANDON"},
        "9588": {"synopsis":"The next file.","comment":"The count back"},
        "9589": {"comment":"The next file"},
        "9591": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "9716": {"synopsis":"One byte of the long name, up to and including its $FF.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9739": {"comment":"and the type's 3 characters"},
        "9744": {"comment":"The last character"},
        "9745": {"comment":"A '.' (no type)?"},
        "9748": {"comment":"Yes: overwritten"},
        "9750": {"comment":"No: kept"},
        "9751": {"synopsis":"The $FF after the name.","comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "9800": {"comment":"\" files copied\", two ENTERs"},
        "9806": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $17"},
        "9811": {"synopsis":"Releases the memory a sorted DOS_CATALOG took: ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG ($011E) with B = 2, C =\n$20 and A = 0 (an unsorted call, as the API document advises), DE = $F700, HL = $E090.\nExit: what DOS_CATALOG returns.","comment":"B = 2 slots, C = $20 (A's filter)"},
        "9814": {"comment":"A = 0: no sorting"},
        "9815": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "9818": {"comment":"The name"},
        "9821": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CATALOG"},
        "9825": {"synopsis":"Copies one file, the source named at $E090 and the destination at $D827 (bank 7, $FF-ended):\nSCR_CT = $FF. Unless $D7FD bit 7 is set the source's name and \" --> \" are printed, and the\ndestination's name and ENTER after it.\n1. The source opened as file 0 for reading (ROM 2's DOS_OPEN: BC = $0001, DE = $0002), the\n   destination as file 1 for writing (BC = $0102, DE = $0204); COPY_DATA copies the bytes;\n   file 1 closed; $D7FE + 1.\n2. When the source has a metadata file (ROM 2's META_NAME builds its name at $F700), it is\n   copied too: opened as file 0, the destination's metadata name built, its directories made\n   (ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS), opened as file 1, COPY_DATA, file 1 closed.\nA failure goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"$FF"},
        "9827": {"comment":"SCR_CT: no 'scroll?'"},
        "9842": {"comment":"\" --> \""},
        "9848": {"synopsis":"The source opened as file 0.","comment":"The source"},
        "9851": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9854": {"comment":"Open action 2 (no header), create action 0"},
        "9857": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9860": {"synopsis":"A failed open or close goes to DOS_FAIL.","comment":"Failed: DOS_FAIL"},
        "9910": {"comment":"The source's name"},
        "9913": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME: its metadata file's name"},
        "9916": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "9918": {"comment":"File 0, exclusive-read"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Open action 2, create action 0"},
        "9924": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9927": {"comment":"Not there: done"},
        "9932": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_NAME"},
        "9935": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9937": {"comment":"None: file 0 closed"},
        "9939": {"comment":"ROM 2's META_MAKE_DIRS: its directories"},
        "9942": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "9944": {"comment":"Failed: file 0 closed"},
        "9946": {"comment":"File 1, exclusive-write"},
        "9949": {"comment":"Open action 4, create action 2"},
        "9952": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "9955": {"comment":"Opened: the bytes copied"},
        "9958": {"comment":"File 1"},
        "9960": {"synopsis":"File B closed.","comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "9967": {"comment":"Yes: no ENTER"},
        "9968": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER through ROM 3's PRINT_A in bank 0, then pages bank 7 back in.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9973": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9976": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"Copies file 0 into file 1 in 2K pieces through $F700 (bank 7), showing the K copied so far:\na space, then for each piece the count (PRINT_K_SIZE, six characters), read by ROM 2's\nDOS_READ ($0112: B = 0, C = 7, DE = $0800) and written by DOS_WRITE ($0115: B = 1, C = 7);\nthe count is backspaced over before the next. The file's end (error $19) closes file 0 and\nwrites what was read; a piece shorter than 2K ends the copy.\nExit: carry when done; NC with A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A space before the count"},
        "9982": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "9985": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9991": {"comment":"The count of K, 0"},
        "9996": {"synopsis":"One piece: the count (HL high word, DE low word, in K) printed.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "9998": {"comment":"BCDE = the count"},
        "10000": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "10003": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10006": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "10009": {"comment":"File 0, into bank 7"},
        "10012": {"comment":"2K"},
